#!build/cubical
-- lib/walk.cub — the onboarding cut into the chunks an agent reads one at a time (Avik, 2026-11-15:
-- every agent reads the same material, whole, in the same order). The documents are the value
-- `onboarding` (docs/onboarding.cub) as the machine evaluates it: a file named by a document is read
-- whole; a projection is the text its value computes. Each document is cut at its paragraphs into
-- chunks of at most w-chunk bytes, a heading opening a chunk once the one before it is half full; a
-- paragraph longer than a chunk is cut at its lines. The chunks are kept in the store (walk/1 …,
-- walk/count), stamped with the time of the latest change under the repository (walk/stamp), and
-- lib/hyperactive.cub serves them; this program runs when the stamp has moved.
import "host.cub"
import "../docs/onboarding.cub"

